NOT RUN (the person who wrote the sheet)
  - Day VWAP: the video's day VWAP starts 18:00 ET. The engine's morning instance reads the trade date's bars from 00:00 ET, so the day VWAP here starts at 00:00 ET (the first six evening hours are missing).
  - London VWAP: no clock time was said; 03:00 ET (08:00 London, 02:00 Central) is my reading.
  - 'Which VWAP is most respected' is a look at the chart with no rule: each VWAP is run alone as its own sheet.
  - 'Away' is not a number in the video: the setting is mine (ticks away from VWAP before a return counts); three values are run as three sheets and none is picked.
  - Skipping sideways days has no rule and is not run (no filter). The Bookmap liquidity check is not run (he says to skip it: 'just take the trade').
  - The 'bad feeling' early exit and the swing-low liquidity sweep trade are not run.
  - The limit order is re-priced at every bar close of the sheet's bar size (1 or 5 minutes), not continuously. A limit fills on a one-tick trade-through (a touch to the tick is no fill): his own fills may be easier.
  - max_trades 5 a pass is mine (the video gives no cap); sessions are separate passes, so a cap counts inside each pass.
  - The video's market is ES; costs are the engine's own (1 tick of slippage on market and stop fills, $4 a round turn).

ALSO TRUE OF THE RUN (the lane)
  - CAPPED PER SESSION PASS, NOT PER DAY: max_trades 5 counts inside each pass (3 passes: nyam, mid, pm), so a day can hold up to 15 trades; a family's own loss or trade count (none) counts inside one pass too.
  - The passes are independent: a trade of one pass may still be open when another pass enters (one position at a time holds inside a pass only).
  - Every trade is flat by 15:58 ET (13:13 on an equity half day); no entry in the last 5 minutes of a pass.
  - Costs: $4.00 a round turn and 1 tick of slippage on market and stop fills, 1 contract (the engine's own).

HONEST LIMITS
  - One video's rule, read on the build days (2021-09-22 .. 2025-06-30): in-sample.
  - The family's settings and the exits are the video's own: nothing was tuned, searched or picked.
  - The neighbours are shown to see how fragile the rule is; they are not alternatives to choose from.
  - The unseen days (2025-07-01 on) were not read: a person has to ask for that, and it is read once.
  - The random entries are the pipeline's own (any bar of the session pass, matched by day and pass): they do not wait for the family's entry window.
NEXT: This is the rule as taught, in-sample. The unseen days are read once, and only when a person asks for it.
